meta {
  name: Tenant vault credentials
  seq: 91
}

docs {
  > Tenant-level model-provider credentials (issue #708). Run the folder in order; `01-` stores
  > `TENANT_CRED_ID` / `TENANT_CRED_NAME` for the later requests.
  >
  > Prerequisites: the default session is a tenant admin (TA). `SPACE_USER_ACCESS_TOKEN` is a
  > non-admin tenant user's token. `PROVIDER_CRED_ID` / `PROVIDER_CRED_NAME` is a space credential an
  > enabled model provider already uses (for `20-`). `21-` needs an OpenAI provider enabled on
  > `TENANT_CRED_NAME`: run `tenant-model-provider/upsert-provider-with-tenant-credential-cross-space.bru`
  > first, and do not run `tenant-model-provider/legacy-provider-flag.bru` between that and `21-`
  > (it moves the OpenAI provider onto a space credential, so `21-` would delete the credential).
  > `22-` and `28-` call the LLM pipeline (`LLMPIPELINE_API_BASE_URL`) as the non-admin user.
}
